    c19_count_night: {
      chapter: "c19",
      location: "Wherever you can lock",
      speaker: "",
      pages: [
        "Night, if the clocks agree, is a lock and a count. You count because counting is armed. Live test: complete, contaminated, or empty. Client: signed, embarrassed, awake. Firms: both still standing, both still calling your code. War: rebranded as concluded. Zero: paused ball, warm door. Voss: metal, sandwich, wall. Kane: invoice, drawer, mint. Vale: feature, margin, instrument. Crowe: rooms, hunt, fruit that bruises. Radek: threshold, sleep, code. Lila: not. Maren: four minutes. Ives: a band, a vote, a daughter who is right. Mia: a joke or a door or a silence.\n\nYour body: used, spent, run, or all three in layers like plates. The rewrite sits where it sits. The flinch sits where it sits. The owned mark, if you took it from Zero, hums like a bracelet you did not clasp. The double, if you are one, aches on a schedule.",
        "You sleep in pieces. You dream the moth on the door lays eggs that are switches. You dream Kane's drawer floods with rain that was printed. You dream Voss subtracts a part she needs and leaves it anyway. You dream Zero lets the ball land and the sound is a name. You wake and check the lock. It holds or it is a van or it is a suite. Holding is not safety. You take it.\n\nAt the edge of sleep you say {{name}} and the vowels do not belong to Ives, not entirely, not yet. Entirely is Vale's metric. Yet is Crowe's. You live in the hitch between them. The hitch is not a country. It is a walk. Walks can still change direction if the plate has a stair. A pipe ticks in the wall like a second clock. You do not synchronize. Disagreement is still a self.",
      ],
      next: "c19_dawn_mark",
    },

    c19_dawn_mark: {
      chapter: "c19",
      location: "Morning · civic resolve",
      speaker: "",
      pages: [
        "Dawn is civic resolve again, smoke gold, focus groups fed. You dress in cloth that may still be lying or in Voss's coat that tells a truer story. You eat. You drink water you have decided to trust. You put a pistol where a pistol goes if you have one. You leave the silver band if it is a claim and take it if it is a courtesy you can spend as metal. Objects, campaign.\n\nThe city looks edible from whatever height you have. It also looks like pulp. Both are true. A tram takes people to work as if work were still a civilian word. You take the tram or a car or a wall. Collection will happen. You have learned to meet it standing. Bread crumbs stay on your cuff. You leave them. Crumbs are proof you ate as a person and not as a vial.",
        "A message from Zero, last, clean grammar: They will ask you to hold a switch. Holding is how they teach ownership. You can hold it for me, for Voss, for Kane, for yourself. Yourself is the one they don't budget. Budget it anyway. I paused the ball. I can drop it if you say so. Say so in a room without a reflection. Maren lives in reflections. I live in a loop. You live in a hitch. I have decided I like the hitch. Don't tell Vale. He will try to dose it.\n\nYou type a word or you don't. The tram leans. Plate Nine slides by, laundry still on lines, annex a dark tooth, arcade glass replaced already because the Stack cannot stand a hole that looks like journalism. You check exits. You have always checked exits. The trivia is now a life.",
      ],
      next: "c19_threshold",
    },

    c19_threshold: {
      chapter: "c19",
      location: "Helix · security cage approach",
      speaker: "",
      pages: [
        "The cage is not on the wellness tour. It sits under the conversion wing the way a conscience sits under a launch: denied, funded, guarded. Radek's people. Vale's key. Crowe's permission if she is in a room-trusting mood. Kane's hunger. Voss's metal. Zero's fear, if completed subjects are allowed fear when a switch comes to visit.\n\nYou stand in the approach corridor and feel last night's religions on you like scents: performance, sabotage, flight. None of them wash off in civic resolve. That is fine. You were not built to be clean. You were recruited because you still had a self. The self is thinner. It is not gone. Thinner is a gait with a hitch. You have practiced. The corridor paint is newer than the wing above, a renovation that wants to look like conscience. You do not believe paint.",
        "Lila passes with a tray that is only a tray. She does not wink. Winks are slides. Her eyes do the heresy. Voss, somewhere, is ugly and near. Kane's mint is a rumor in a vent. Maren's reflection ticks in a pane. You step toward the cage because the campaign's next hour is a kill-switch and because standing here is how statues get measured for plazas.\n\nYour name, in your mouth, one more time before the feature: {{name}}. It holds. It shakes. It is still the resource they cannot clone cheaply. Not yet. Yet is a clock that disagrees with other clocks. You walk while the disagreement lasts. The tray in Lila's hands is empty and still looks heavy. Empty can be heavy. You file that for the cage. A camera above the approach blinks. You give it the hitch and nothing else.",
      ],
      next: "c19_end",
    },

    c19_end: {
      chapter: "c19",
      location: "Outside the cage",
      speaker: "",
      journal: "The live test closed. The switch opened a mouth.",
      pages: [
        "Outside the cage the air is colder, honest as a receipt. A camera does not bother to hide. You look into it and do not smile Zero's exactness. You give it the hitch. Let the waveform end in a color Vale did not order. Let Ives's committee see a person if Maren allows. Let Crowe call it precious. Precious people break. You have been breaking in a controlled way for twenty chapters of weather.\n\nRadek unlocks, or Voss picks, or Kane bills a key, or Vale simply arrives with the face of a man who built a god he does not trust. The door makes a sound like a tray dropping. You think of Lila. You think of water. You think of a dog that never lands and a ball you could drop.\n\nInside there will be a switch. Outside there is still a city. You go in because out is a map with water damage and in is a fact. Kane told you to die, if you must, on a fact. You do not intend to die. Intention is a distressed asset. You spend it anyway.",
        "The live test is over. The proof, whatever it was, is already a lullaby in Crowe's mouth and a drink in Voss's and a clip in Maren's and a margin in Vale's and a paused loop in Zero's. You are the remainder. Remainders are how math admits a self.\n\nYou cross the threshold. The campaign, which is not a demo, which is a long novel if you read it like a book, turns the page onto a feature called kill. You keep your vowels in your own throat. You keep the hitch. You keep the paper flower in the walk. The cage light is kind in Vale's way. You do not thank it. You go to see who gets to end a country, and whether the hand that holds the ending can still belong to {{name}}. The door seals behind you with a courtesy click. Courtesy is Vale's kindness. You do not return it. You keep your hands empty and your hitch intact.",
      ],
      next: "c20_start",
    },
